---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import sarahPhoto from '../assets/sarah.png';
---

<Layout
  title="About Sarah — Licensed Massage Therapist in Grand County, CO"
  description="Meet Sarah, the licensed massage therapist behind Chaos & Chemistry. Exercise Science degree, Costa Rica School of Massage Therapy graduate, Colorado License #MT.0026235."
>
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 grid md:grid-cols-[2fr_3fr] gap-12 items-start">
      <div>
        <Image
          src={sarahPhoto}
          alt="Sarah, licensed massage therapist (Colorado MT.0026235)"
          class="rounded-2xl shadow-lg w-full aspect-square object-cover"
          widths={[300, 500, 700]}
          sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 400px"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="text-sage-600 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs mb-3">Meet the Therapist</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-sage-900 mb-6">Hi, I'm Sarah.</h1>

        <div class="prose prose-lg text-sage-800 space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I've called Grand County home since 2019, when I finished my Exercise Science
            degree at Slippery Rock University and moved west. After several years working
            across the valley, I fulfilled a long-held dream and graduated from the
            <strong>Costa Rica School of Massage Therapy</strong> in 2023.
          </p>

          <p>
            My approach blends my exercise science background with an integrated bodywork
            practice — Swedish, deep tissue, myofascial release, trigger point therapy,
            cupping, and craniosacral techniques all woven together to meet your body where
            it is.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also have a deep passion for energy work, and I aim to create a grounded,
            nurturing space where each client is invited to come home to their body through
            breathwork and mindfulness during their session.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 bg-sage-100 border border-sage-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-sm text-sage-800">
          <p class="font-medium text-sage-900 mb-2">Credentials</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside marker:text-sage-500">
            <li>Colorado Licensed Massage Therapist (MT.0026235)</li>
            <li>BS, Exercise Science — Slippery Rock University</li>
            <li>Costa Rica School of Massage Therapy, 2023</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-sage-100 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-sage-900 mb-6">My Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-sage-800 leading-relaxed">
        There is chaos and chemistry reflected in every area of existence — from the stars
        in the cosmos to the cells in the human body. Massage and bodywork are how I help
        clients quiet some of that chaos and find their own rhythm again.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
